Regulatory risk refers to *uncertainty surrounding actions by a governmental entity.* An example of regulatory risk could be a change in tax law or margin requirements that alters the payoff for a given trade.

In practice it is very close to #voir("legal-risk").

They are highly integrated with both #voir("operational-risk") and #voir("reputation-risk"). 